{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ah give me a second, this yoke is after freezing again. Right. What's brought you in?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): I'm wrecked, if you want the truth. I wake up in a sweat and I'm shaking like a leaf, every morning. It's doing me head in.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sweating and the shakes, every morning. How long is that going on?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm. A couple of weeks. Maybe three. I'm not counting, it just...",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): And in the morning, do you get any breakfast into you before you...",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't bother. Never have. A cup of tea and I'm gone. I'm not hungry, doctor, don't start on me.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): Grand. Any dizziness with it?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No dizziness. I'm not dizzy.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, say that again there, the screen jumped.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): I said I'm not dizzy. Can we move on. I was stuck in that waiting room an age.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right so. I need the tablets off you again, doses and all. The list on here is a mess.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): The sugar tablets, for me sugar. Gliklazide 80 milligrams in the morning. And the metforman, I thought it was 500 but no, it's the big ones, a gram twice a day.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Hold on. The metformin, say it again. A gram twice a day, is it?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): A thousand milligrams, twice a day. With the dinner and at night. Supposed to be with food, I know, I know.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): And besides those two?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Amlodopine 5 milligrams in the morning, for the pressure. The cholesterol one at night, atorvastin 20, for the cholesterol. Only the Ayurvedic powder in the morning as well, a spoon of it in water.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): The powder. Have you any notion what's in it?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Haven't a notion. My sister got it in the health shop. She swears by the stuff.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Okay. Any chest pain with these morning turns?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Your waiting room is freezing, I'll say that. And the fella on the desk hadn't a clue...",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): The chest, though. Pain? Or short of breath?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No chest pain. Breathing is grand. I'm just tired and ratty, that's all.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Has anyone noticed you confused at all, or did you black out?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Blacked out, no. My daughter was in last week. She said I was confused the once, didn't know the day, and she was right. I was away with it that morning and then it lifted.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Was that the same morning as the sweating, or a different...",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): She brought scones. I didn't even want them. She's terrible fussy about the tea.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, I asked was it the same morning.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. The one morning, with the sweats. Not since.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mm. Anything else you've thought of?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Actually, no, I told you I wasn't dizzy and that's not right. The head goes light every morning with the shakes. I have to sit on the bed till it eases.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right, that fits together. I think your sugar is dropping in the mornings, the gliclazide on an empty stomach. Working impression only, mind you.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): So I'm not losing the plot. What are you doing about it, then.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Eat something before that gliclazide. Even a bit of toast, don't skip the breakfast. I'm leaving the doses as they are today.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Toast. Grand. If I remember.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll book the bloods, the HbA1c and a kidney check. Come back in a fortnight when they're in and we'll go through them.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): A fortnight. Right. Can I go, I'm tired of this."
 ],
